      "message": "I\u0027m finally realizing that Graphite\u0027s [`VULKAN_CALL_xyz` macros](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanGraphiteUtilsPriv.h) receive a `VulkanInterface` which just has Vk function pointers but no state, whereas Ganesh\u0027s [analogous macros](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/ganesh/vk/GrVkUtil.h) receive a `GrVkGpu` argument, allowing them to check device lost state and call `checkVkResult`.\n\nWould it be feasible to update Graphite\u0027s `VULKAN_CALL` macros to take `VulkanSharedContext` (instead of `VulkanInterface` directly) in a follow-up CL? (Asking architecturally, but also because I don\u0027t want to block Ganesh using this callback on that.)",
